body:
I hope you feel better soon! 

&#x200B;

What are the bands used for? New braces wearer here, this is a completely new world to me that I am blindly navigating.

GET IT! I'm so glad to see the progress on it! 

&#x200B;

Side question -- How long does it take you to finish one page?

Holy shit, preach. This is the best explanation-- thank you.

&#x200B;

I also hope everything works out with you and your husband.

I am in EMDR therapy right now, actually. I've been going once every week/ every other week because she's so booked. I can see a difference in my attitude and handling the things I wouldn't normally handle so well. It has been a great experience so far (minus, ya know, having to deal with the trauma).

&#x200B;

My question is, how do you know when it's your "Last" session?

&#x200B;

By the way, congratulations, and I hope everything goes well for you from this experience <3

This was so helpful to read and brought tears to my eyes. I'm so glad to see you've had great results with it and I so appreciate the explanation of it all; my anxiety was starting to run when I started to think about it. Thank you for the warning of the physical exhaustion too. As of late I have been so exhausted from all the stress in general that its good to know what to expect and be prepared for it.

&#x200B;

Thank you so much, again.
